{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335834-what-would-the-chronicles-of-darkness-planescape-be-like","id":1335834,"title":"What would the Chronicles of Darkness Planescape be like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-14T20:37:56-07:00","id":1335834,"title":"What would the Chronicles of Darkness Planescape be like?","content":"The title is the thread.<br /> <br /> I recently read a review of a Planescape-alike, largely narrative-focused game called <i>Sig: Manual of the Primes</i>, and wow. I didn't fully comprehend how weird and wild the concept of Ideological Planes could be when not relying on the Good-Evil-Law-Chaos axis. In fact, one might say that the Planes in that setting transcend the concept of alignment, because they're nothing but roots of political philosophy; the Ideological Plane of Tyranny, for instance, is a cosmos-sized prison geared towards convincing its inmates that <i>this is right, this is what leads to perfect law, </i>and those who accept this lesson sprout horns and become Devahil, the demonic enforcers of justice without doubt. The Conceptual Plane of Shadows hunger for new ideas to tell it what to be, a place of perfect illusions and sublime ambitions - for the realm of illusion contains the concepts of Fiction and Invention within it, as those are ways of turning what is simply thought into a more constant reality. It's a damn weird setting, and I love it.<br /> <br /> Which is what set me off, as I remembered a long, long-ago thread that attempted to make NWoD Planescape - you can't find that thread now, it was literally two iterations of this board ago. But I remembered how interesting that was as an idea, and how I liked their idea of the City Between Realities as a ruined place of chaos - there are enforcers, but they only keep the city itself barely functioning, as gangs of would-be Tyrants try to use the portals as staging grounds to carve personal fiefdoms out of the cosmos, all while everyone else is trying to get back home and understand this weird new multiverse. I felt the idea died before it could be refined into something playable or good, but Sig provided both a stable setting beyond the city, that always involves the planes outside it somehow (what parts of the major planes attached to the city change it to fit themselves, not the least because for as long as the Tether lasts, descendants and natives of the Tethered plane benefit from a universal translator effect, making them the heart of the government managing to somehow function until the Tether is shifted), as well as a mechanic any revised version of Planescape needs - the ability to form your personal portal, at the cost of a bit of yourself (forming an artificial Portal Pool requires sacrificing an important relationship to the city as a price - your best friend forgets who you are, your spouse moves out and files for divorce, your child comes to see you as a toxic, abusive mess and cuts you loose).<br /> <br /> Plus, if nothing else, it did give the hypothetical setting something of a true overarching antagonist faction: a demiplane formed from the intersection of Tyranny, Order, and Justice, to become the Eternal Empire - the very concept of expansionism and colonialism made into its own pocket world, the shining capital of a multiversal state for whom the entire cosmos is a savage wilderness begging to be civilized, tamed, and exploited for all its worth. And like most empires, it's always happy to accept those barbarians who see the light that their culture provides the worlds as local governors...<br /> <br /> I can see myself adapting the Sworn rules for this, with the players being a newly-formed faction trying to make their own ideological mark on the multiverse - which also means delicately balancing patrons, winning over skeptical allies, matching wits with rival gods, and worst of all, <i>properly filing the paperwork for authorization</i>. Wars have been started to shift Tethers to a faction's native plane just so they can actually read the goddamned forms.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. What about you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-15-2019, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T17:41:21-07:00","id":1336125,"title":"","content":"I missed Planescape entirely, in its time. However, when I picked up the Manual of Planes for 4E (a game my group played primarily as a comparatively casual tactical war game and enjoyed enough to continue doing so for about three years), I was pleasantly surprised by how much world-building was in it for a game that was laser-focused on combat. Based on your descriptions, it sounds like most of the ideas for planes were ripped straight out of Planescape. So, gone but not forgotten, as it were (and certainly not by the people who own the intellectual property rights for it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:30:21-07:00","id":1336595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335834-what-would-the-chronicles-of-darkness-planescape-be-like#post1335834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recently read a review of a Planescape-alike, largely narrative-focused game called <i>Sig: Manual of the Primes</i>, and wow. I didn't fully comprehend how weird and wild the concept of Ideological Planes could be when not relying on the Good-Evil-Law-Chaos axis. In fact, one might say that the Planes in that setting transcend the concept of alignment, because they're nothing but roots of political philosophy; the Ideological Plane of Tyranny, for instance, is a cosmos-sized prison geared towards convincing its inmates that <i>this is right, this is what leads to perfect law, </i>and those who accept this lesson sprout horns and become Devahil, the demonic enforcers of justice without doubt. The Conceptual Plane of Shadows hunger for new ideas to tell it what to be, a place of perfect illusions and sublime ambitions - for the realm of illusion contains the concepts of Fiction and Invention within it, as those are ways of turning what is simply thought into a more constant reality. It's a damn weird setting, and I love it.</div> </div> </div> </div> What you describe here is pretty much what the Astral Space of MtAw and the Astral Reaches of MTAs are. So not only would it fit into the WoD, it already exists^^.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T11:11:27-07:00","id":1336602,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'd go with Mage's Supernal Emanations for this rather than Astral Space. Just stay away from any Emanations of Tyranny; the Exarchs will have you for lunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T12:23:18-07:00","id":1336620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335834-what-would-the-chronicles-of-darkness-planescape-be-like?p=1336602#post1336602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I'd go with Mage's Supernal Emanations for this rather than Astral Space. Just stay away from any Emanations of Tyranny; the Exarchs will have you for lunch.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really wouldn't. I understand emanations as connected to Supernal Realms and the symbology of the Arcana. In that they embodiment of the symbols that ruele the Supernal Realms and their connected Arcana.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the Astral Space, well before I write something up myself:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;This is where individual souls coalesce into the massed soul of Humanity, private thoughts becoming shared myths, archetypes, and concepts. They cluster by theme. Realms of Fascism, Collectivism, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Democracy belong to the greater realms of Government, and share territory with Human Nature. You can meet every god here, every fiction, and even people so famous they fill the mythic roles of old deities. Temenos conceptual realms include every magical tradition ever practiced by more than one person. Various regions belong to Paths, Orders, Legacies, and other cults.&quot;</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T14:37:39-07:00","id":1336668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335834-what-would-the-chronicles-of-darkness-planescape-be-like?p=1336620#post1336620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really wouldn't. I understand emanations as connected to Supernal Realms and the symbology of the Arcana. In that they embodiment of the symbols that ruele the Supernal Realms and their connected Arcana.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the Astral Space, well before I write something up myself:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;This is where individual souls coalesce into the massed soul of Humanity, private thoughts becoming shared myths, archetypes, and concepts. They cluster by theme. Realms of Fascism, Collectivism, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Democracy belong to the greater realms of Government, and share territory with Human Nature. You can meet every god here, every fiction, and even people so famous they fill the mythic roles of old deities. Temenos conceptual realms include every magical tradition ever practiced by more than one person. Various regions belong to Paths, Orders, Legacies, and other cults.&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned Emanations of Tyranny and the Exarchs for a reason: the Supernal isn't <i>just</i> the Arcana. You can have Supernal Emanations that don't conform to the ten Arcana that Mage puts front and center; and you can have Supernal Emanations that only cover a portion of what a full Arcanum covers. An Emanation of Shadows might be a \u201csubset\u201d of Death (the Arcanum that covers darkness and shadows), or it might be tied to a part of the Supernal that deals with shadows in a manner different from how Death deals with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-26-2019, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T20:22:35-07:00","id":1336754,"title":"","content":"Emanation Realms also came to my mind. Elemental planes and heavens and hells are specifically mentioned in Signs as examples, and strike me as shoe in for what D&amp;D-ish outer planes might be like. Beasts strike me as ideal characters for such a chronicle as well.<br /> <br /> You can use astral realms of course, but the locals tend to be a bit... lackluster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T21:17:58-07:00","id":1336765,"title":"","content":"The main problem with Astral Space is that, by and large, it can only be visited through some sort of astral projection: you can't go there physically. There are are exceptions (in the Chronicles of Darkness, there are <i>always</i> exceptions); but the rule is that Astral Space isn't physical. Go to an Emanation of Shadows, and you're in a realm of Shadows made manifest; go to an Astral Realm of Shadows, and you're in what amounts to a \u201cdream of Shadows\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T17:22:45-07:00","id":1338077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335834-what-would-the-chronicles-of-darkness-planescape-be-like?p=1336765#post1336765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem with Astral Space is that, by and large, it can only be visited through some sort of astral projection: you can't go there physically. There are are exceptions (in the Chronicles of Darkness, there are <i>always</i> exceptions); but the rule is that Astral Space isn't physical. Go to an Emanation of Shadows, and you're in a realm of Shadows made manifest; go to an Astral Realm of Shadows, and you're in what amounts to a \u201cdream of Shadows\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div> Beasts, Demons, and Helldivers can get to the Astral Plane Physically and take others with them. I don't know if mages a have spell that can do that, perhaps space + mind + life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T17:55:49-07:00","id":1338084,"title":"","content":"I will point out the a goetic reflection of Sigil would exist in the Astral Plane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T03:48:45-07:00","id":1338123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335834-what-would-the-chronicles-of-darkness-planescape-be-like?p=1338077#post1338077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts, Demons, and Helldivers can get to the Astral Plane Physically and take others with them. I don't know if mages a have spell that can do that, perhaps space + mind + life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Teleportation (Space 4) with conjunctional Mind 2 should suffice.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another way would be to create an Iris that allows bodies through. Mind 5 with conjunctional Space. I could see anything from Space 2 to Space 5 being required for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-27-2019, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T21:18:14-07:00","id":1339990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335834-what-would-the-chronicles-of-darkness-planescape-be-like?p=1338077#post1338077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts, Demons, and Helldivers can get to the Astral Plane Physically and take others with them. I don't know if mages a have spell that can do that, perhaps space + mind + life?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that physical travel to the Astral Realms of impossible; I said that it's the exception. And the nature of that exception is that it's not technically \u201cphysical travel\u201d; it's more akin to entering the digital world of Tron: the traveler gets transformed into a being composed of the same essence as is found in Astral Space. <br /> <br /> Astral Space is an \u201cinner space\u201d \u2014 the landscape of the mind and the soul. It includes peoples' dreams and their personal soulscapes \u2014 the Oneiroi that Mage talks about. It's possible to treat it as a physical place; but that's not the role that it was designed to serve. <br /> <br /> By contrast, Emanations are physical places where concepts are made manifest. Elemental Planes, Realms where Tyranny is something tangible, and things like that are precisely what Emanations exist to represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}